PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H}

The question asks for the *least* plausible explanation among the eight choices for the consistent blank circles in the Kunoichi no Jutsu section.  

After reviewing each option against the known history of the Bansenshukai (a 1676 compilation by Fujibayashi, widely copied in the Edo period, with all surviving manuscripts showing identical lacunae), H stands out as the most speculative and internally inconsistent. It conflates Kuji-in hand seals with “nine holes,” Taoist sexual alchemy, and chakra lore; it invents an erotic-ritual layer for which there is no documentary trace in any ninjutsu text; and it misreads the ⬤/○ notation itself as a failed transcription of those seals rather than a deliberate placeholder. The remaining options, while varying in historical probability, at least rest on attested practices (secrecy, moral censorship, physical wear, aburidashi, oral mnemonics, or political redaction). H therefore requires the largest number of unsupported assumptions and is the least plausible.

